@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# Retrospective transcript summary, backfilled for issue #355 (full backfill
# follow-up to the #352 sample), distilling PR #196's own body/commit history --
# no live session context was available (this PR predates or was outside this
# backfill session), per docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md's
# retrospective case. Timestamps are real, from `gh pr view 196 --json
# commits,mergedAt`: startedAtTime is the first commit's authoredDate, endedAtTime is the PR's actual mergedAt.

ghpull:196 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "fix(tests): load W3C manifests as RDF via turtle+sparql_parser, not line-scanning" ;
    bl:number 196 ;
    bl:state bl:Closed ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:192 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr196 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:192 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-07-20T17:57:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-07-20T19:33:07Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr196Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Fixes #192. The W3C SPARQL 1.1 conformance harness (tests/w3c_sparql11_suite.rs) parsed manifest.ttl fixtures with a hand-rolled, line-oriented mini-parser that tracked mf:action [ ... ] block state per *line*. Since the dominant style in this vendored corpus puts mf:action alone on its own line with [ qt:query ... starting on the next line, in_action_block never turned on for these entries and the whole entry was silently dropped — every currently-wired eval-test suite (bind, exists, bindings, subquery, aggregates, negation, property-path, construct, functions, grouping, project-expression) was executing zero real QueryEvaluationTest assertions while reporting ok. This is broader than the issue's own estimate (which focused on negation): a full audit found no manifest in this corpus with [ on the same line as qt:query, so the bug affected 100% of block-style eval entries, not just a fraction. Fix approach Per direction from review, replaced the line-scanning parser entirely with an RDF-native loader, rather than patching the line-tracking state machine: 1. Parse manifest.ttl as real Turtle (turtle::parse_turtle_with_base, using file://<canonicalized manifest path> as the base IRI so relative <file.rq> references resolve to real absolute filesystem paths) into a dag_rdf::Datastore. 2." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:196 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr196 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
